course: dictionary
lesson: 4629
title: Where is it? Words for places
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A hillside is the sloping side of a hill. It is not the top of the hill, and it is not the flat land at the bottom. Think of the part you climb up or walk down.
explain: Authors use hillside to tell us where something is. «The Sermon on the Mount is Jesus' great teaching on a hillside.» The word hillside tells you the place: the teaching happened on the slope, not at the top of the hill or in a town.
explain: Read the words around it for clues. «A border collie herds sheep by running around them and bringing them to the shepherd, who guides the dog with whistles that carry far across a hillside.» The whistles carry far across the slope, so a hillside is a wide, open place. Check your meaning: swap in "the sloping side of a hill" and the sentence still makes sense.
fact: A hillside is the sloping side of a hill.
fact: Hillside is a noun, and its plural is hillsides.
fact: Hillside tells you where something is: sheep on the hillside, houses on the hillside, a path up the hillside.
fact: A steep hillside can be slippery, and in heavy rain mud can slide down it.
exercise: «The Sermon on the Mount is Jesus' great teaching on a hillside.» Where did the teaching happen? | *On the slope of a hill | In a shop | Inside a castle | At the bottom of the sea
exercise: Mia says a hillside is the top of the hill. What is a hillside? | A kind of hill-shaped cake | *The sloping side of a hill | The top of the hill, flat and round | The flat land by the river
exercise: Why can a steep hillside be dangerous in heavy rain? | Because the sheep will be wet | Because hillsides are always made of sand | Because the sun is too hot | *Because it can be slippery and mud can slide down it
test: «The shepherd's whistles carried far across a hillside.» Where did the whistles carry? | Inside a house | Under the sea | In a cave | *Across the slope of a hill
test: «Bears dig winter dens under tree roots, in hillsides or under snow.» Where can bears dig their dens? | On a busy road | *In the sloping side of a hill | Up in the sky | In the middle of a lake
exam: Which sentence uses hillside to tell us where something is? | *Sheep grazed on the hillside | Hillside is a noun | Hillsides are big and green | The hillside was steep and slippery
